@@ -447,6 +447,10 @@ The library also supports convenient formatting of ranges and tuples::
   fmt::print("{}", t);
 
 
+Nested ranges are formatted recursively, with characters and strings quoted and
+escaped by default. This also applies to C++20 range views, including views that
+produce temporary ranges with non-const ``begin()`` and ``end()``.
+
 NOTE: currently, the overload of ``fmt::join`` for iterables exists in the main
 ``format.h`` header, but expect this to change in the future.
 
